From 8829fd2ffee544c910f2b47f6b054d80f39ec30f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:01:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: clear the MST bits in mainlink control for an SST
 stream

The MST enable bits in DP_MAINLINK_CTRL are only ever set on stream on,
and are cleared only when link training fails. Taking the link down
after an MST session (msm_dp_ctrl_off_link()) keeps them, and the
mainlink enable that follows is a read-modify-write, so the next SST
sink is driven with MST framing: link training passes but the stream
never starts ("wait4video timedout").

Program the bits from mst_active on every stream on.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
index e6f64f389..28cd18a93 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -2965,8 +2965,7 @@ int msm_dp_ctrl_on_stream(struct msm_dp_ctrl *msm_dp_ctrl, struct msm_dp_panel *
 
 	msm_dp_ctrl_lane_mapping(ctrl);
 	msm_dp_setup_peripheral_flush(ctrl);
-	if (ctrl->mst_active)
-		msm_dp_ctrl_mst_config(ctrl, true);
+	msm_dp_ctrl_mst_config(ctrl, ctrl->mst_active);
 
 	msm_dp_ctrl_configure_source_params(ctrl, panel);
 
-- 
